search index=vpn sourcetype=f5:bigip:apm:syslog
``` Template: F5 BIG-IP APM VPN denials (Splunk Add-on for F5 BIG-IP). ```
``` Modele : refus de connexion VPN F5 BIG-IP APM (Splunk Add-on for F5 BIG-IP).
    L'IP du client et le refus sont sur deux lignes differentes d'une meme session :
    la recherche regarde 10 min plus tot (lookback_minutes: 10 dans la config) pour
    retrouver l'ouverture de session, puis ne garde que les refus du lot ($WINDOW_START$). ```
| rex field=_raw ":Common:(?<sess>[0-9a-f]+):"
| rex field=_raw "New session from client IP (?<cip>\S+) \("
| rex field=_raw "/Common/Workflow[_-]?(?<portail>[^:]+):"
| eventstats values(cip) as cip, values(portail) as portail by sess
| search "Logon_Deny"
| eval src_ip = mvindex(cip, 0)
| where isnotnull(src_ip) AND _time >= $WINDOW_START$
| eventstats count as rafale by src_ip
| eval severity = case(rafale > 5, "critical", rafale > 2, "high", true(), "medium")
| eval signature = "Refus VPN", dest_host = mvindex(portail, 0), action = "blocked",
       dc = "DC-NORD"
| fields _time, src_ip, Country, src_lat, src_lon, dc, severity, signature, dest_host, action
